Patch 0013 -- loop closing (module 7): id-ordered containers, loop trace, opt-in Eigen solver

Three independent parts; parts 1 and 3 do not change any computed value in a
default run, part 2 is dump-only and off unless the driver enables it.

1. Determinism (order only). The loop-correction path used POINTER-ordered
   containers whose iteration order decides which landmark/keyframe is handled
   first (ASLR-dependent, so two runs of the same binary could differ once a
   loop is accepted):
     * module::keyframe_Sim3_pairs_t  std::map<shared_ptr<keyframe>, Sim3,
       std::less<...>> -> id_less. Iterated by correct_covisibility_landmarks()
       (a landmark seen by several neighbors is corrected with the FIRST
       neighbor in iteration order: found_lm_to_ref_keyfrm_id) and by
       replace_duplicated_landmarks() (neighbor order of the fuse pass).
     * graph_node::get_loop_edges()  std::set<shared_ptr<keyframe>> ->
       id_ordered_set (iterated by graph_optimizer -> edge insertion order).
     * global_optimization_module::extract_new_connections() and
       graph_optimizer::optimize()'s loop_connections: outer map and inner
       sets pointer-ordered -> id-ordered (edge insertion order = g2o edge
       ids = Hessian accumulation order).
   nullptr keys (expired weak_ptr locks in get_connected_keyframes()) sort last
   (id_less semantics), as the DETERMINISTIC aliases already do elsewhere.
   Membership-only containers (keyfrms_to_reject, keyframe_set::keyfrm_set_,
   the already_checked map) are untouched: their order is unobservable.

2. Loop trace (dump only). New util/loop_trace.h (+ globals in
   util/erasure_log.cc): when the driver sets util::g_loop_trace to a FILE*,
   loop_detector, transform_optimizer, graph_optimizer and
   global_optimization_module::{run_step,correct_loop} print one tab separated
   line per event (%a doubles). util::g_loop_hook(phase) is called from
   run_step() with phase 0 before the step, 1 after the pose graph
   optimization, 2 after an accepted loop incl. the loop BA. Extra read-only
   getter data::bow_database::get_all_keyframe_ids().

3. Opt-in solver switch (default OFF). With env STELLA_PORT_EIGEN_SOLVER set,
   graph_optimizer and global_bundle_adjuster use g2o's LinearSolverEigen
   (SimplicialLLT + AMD, the solver the C port reimplements) instead of the
   LGPL CSparse solver. Without the variable behaviour is unchanged.

4. Opt-in threshold overrides (default = upstream constants): env
   STELLA_PORT_LOOP_THR_OPT1 / _A / _B replace the three hard-coded validation
   thresholds of loop_detector::select_loop_candidate_via_Sim3() (10 / 25 / 40),
   so rejection at each later stage can be provoked on real data. The values in
   effect are printed in the CAND trace line; the YAML-configured detector
   parameters are printed in the DET line.

